From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] print control: Kiln's cancel during the print start

Stop while a print starts said the printer finishes its start sequence
and then stops. On Kiln OS the start now ends at its next safe point
(ad5x_soak notes the cancel when it arrives: heating and the bed heat
soak end within a second, a probe, the mesh or a colour load first
finishes), so the AD5X build says that.
---
diff --git a/src/ui/print_control_buttons.cpp b/src/ui/print_control_buttons.cpp
index 09dba91..b5bd7d9 100644
--- a/src/ui/print_control_buttons.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/print_control_buttons.cpp
@@ -320,8 +320,16 @@ void PrintControlButtons::request_sent_start_cancel() {
     auto& ps = get_printer_state().print_state();
     cancel_epoch_ = lv_subject_get_int(ps.get_preparing_epoch_subject());
     ps.note_preparing_cancel_requested();
+#if defined(HELIX_KILN_AD5X)
+    // Kiln OS (AD5X): ad5x_soak notes the cancel when it arrives; the
+    // print start ends at its next safe point (heating and the soak within
+    // a second, a probe or the mesh after it finishes)
+    NOTIFY_INFO(lv_tr("Cancel sent. The printer stops its start sequence at the next safe "
+                      "point."));
+#else
     NOTIFY_INFO(lv_tr("Cancel sent. The printer finishes its start sequence, then stops "
                       "before printing."));
+#endif
     const auto start = ps.preparing_start();
     // A start the printer announced itself is on the printer with no job of ours
     // to wait for.
